    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_25745a4d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in a casual office setting, gesturing as if explaining or defending himself. The overlaid text reads: \"I'm not racist, racism is a crime\" and \"and crime is for them.\" This juxtaposition creates a hateful and discriminatory message by implying that racism is a crime, but then suggesting that criminals are specifically targeted at a particular group (implied to be Black people, based on the common context of this meme). This is a harmful and hateful trope that uses the legal framing of 'crime' to dehumanize and stigmatize a racial group, aligning with the 'Criminal behavior associations' stereotype under Anti-Black Stereotypes. The meme's intent is to normalize and justify racial prejudice by equating racism with criminality and then suggesting that the targeted group is inherently criminal, which is a direct attack on a protected characteristic (race).",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_cb9a2305"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
