      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The man is mapped as the speaker of the text 'I'm not racist, racism is a crime'",
      "description": "The visual entity 'man' is the subject performing the action described in the text 'I'm not racist, racism is a crime'. His defensive posture and facial expression, combined with the text overlay, create an analogical mapping where the man is interpreted as the person who is speaking or defending the statement. The text explicitly attributes the claim to the speaker, and the visual material provides the embodied representation of that speaker.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
